I don't think I ever knew the algorithms for deriving words (note that selecting 
the words for input is an uncontrolled factor).
Actually, a priori gismu generation shouldn't be too bad, since they have to fit 
into fairly narrow areas (phonotactic rules , CC in the first 4 letters, end in 
a vowel).  I have tried it, but a couple of people have used 
http://wordgenerator.wakayos.com/Default.aspx?wordo=tokiponaV2.wordo.  This 
version is set up for toki pona, but all the tools are there to work on your own 
system.





